# R5-3b: three index steps on a three-level own Array -- `t[1]\[0]\[2]: 9`, read back by the same steps; the depth
# is the contract's, no index-count cap; `length(t[1]\[0])` is the innermost level's length.  Before: "own array index
# requires a supported integer expression" / "length requires one known primitive own array".  Natively and with the
# methods walked.  Entry 7.
fn: work () int
    []: []: []: int t 2
    []: []: int m 2
    []: int r 3
    m[0]: r
    t[1]: m
    t[1]\[0]\[2]: 9
    if: r[2] != 9 || t[1]\[0]\[2] != 9
        return: 81
    if: length(t[1]\[0]) != 3U || length(t[1]) != 2U || length(t) != 2U
        return: 82
    return: 7
end: work
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: work(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
